      "message": "I think these release asserts when we overflow the id deserve a padding in a message parameter to clarify why we are falling over in the log (it would either indicate an exceptionally long process up time, or bad app behavior).\n\nI think with 2^63 values for `id`, if we assume 1000 bitmaps generated per frame at 120fps, we\u0027d overflow after 2^63/(1000*120*60*60*24*365) years (~2.4 million). That same scenario with just `uint32_t` would take 5 hours. Given that, I\u0027m certainly okay with crashing in order to guarantee the uniqueness of the IDs.",
